hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22298","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr, meaning al-Raqqi, narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysa, Jabala ibn Suhaym narrated to us, from Abu al-Muthanna al-Abdi, he said: I heard al-Sadusi, meaning Ibn al-Khasasiyya, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to pledge him. He said: So he stipulated upon me testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that I establish prayer, and give zakat, and perform the Hajj of Islam, and fast the month of Ramadan, and strive in the path of Allah. I said: O Messenger of Allah, as for two, by Allah I cannot bear them: jihad and charity, for they claim that whoever turns his back earns anger from Allah, and I fear if I attend that, my soul will panic and hate death, and charity, for by Allah I have nothing but a small flock and ten camels; they are the provision of my family and their mounts. He said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, grasped his hand, then moved his hand, then said: No jihad and no charity, then how will you enter Paradise? He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I pledge you. He said: So I pledged him upon all of them."
"22299","Waki narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to me, from Khalid ibn Sumayr, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Bashir Ibn al-Khasasiyya, the Bashir of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw a man walking in two sandals between the graves and said: O wearer of the Sibtiyya sandals, cast them off."
"22300","Abu al-Walid and Affan said: Ubayd Allah ibn Iyad ibn Laqit narrated to us, I heard Iyad ibn Laqit saying: I heard Layla, the wife of Bashir, saying: Bashir asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Shall I fast Friday and not speak to anyone that day? The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not fast Friday except in days of which it is one of them, or in a month. As for not speaking to anyone, by your life, to speak good and forbid evil is better than to be silent."
"22301","Abu al-Walid and Affan narrated to us, they said: Ubaydullah ibn Iyad narrated to us, Iyad, meaning ibn Laqit, narrated to us, from Layla the wife of Bashir, she said: I wanted to fast two days continuously, so Bashir prevented me and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it and said: The Christians do that. And Affan said: The Christians do that, but fast as Allah, Mighty and Majestic, commanded you, and complete the fast to the night, and when it is night then break the fast."
"22302","Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Iyad ibn Laqit al-Shaybani narrated to us, from his father, from Layla the wife of Bashir ibn al-Khasasiyah, from Bashir, he said, and he had come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: His name was Zahm, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him Bashir."
